Bootstrap is a popular open-source front-end framework developed by Twitter. It provides a collection of CSS, JavaScript, and HTML components that simplify the process of building responsive, mobile-first web applications.

🔑 Key Features
Responsive Grid System: Built on a 12-column layout, enabling flexible design across devices.

Predefined CSS Classes: For typography, buttons, forms, tables, and navigation.

Reusable Components: Modals, dropdowns, carousels, alerts, badges, progress bars.

JavaScript Plugins: Interactive features like tooltips, popovers, collapsible menus.

Customization: Can be tailored using Sass variables or by overriding default styles.

Cross-browser Compatibility: Works consistently across modern browsers.

⚡ Advantages
Rapid development with minimal custom CSS.

Consistent design language across projects.

Strong community support and documentation.

Easy integration with frameworks like Angular, React, and ASP.NET MVC.

🎯 20 Bootstrap Interview Questions & Answers
Basics
What is Bootstrap?  
Bootstrap is a front-end framework that provides pre-styled components and a responsive grid system to speed up web development.

Why is Bootstrap called mobile-first?  
Its grid system and components are designed to adapt to smaller screens first, then scale up for larger devices.

Explain the Bootstrap Grid System.  
It uses a 12-column layout with classes like .col-sm-6, .col-md-4, allowing responsive design by defining column widths per device size.

Difference between Bootstrap 4 and Bootstrap 5?  
Bootstrap 5 dropped jQuery dependency, introduced enhanced grid system, utilities API, and improved form controls.

What are breakpoints in Bootstrap?  
Predefined screen sizes (sm, md, lg, xl, xxl) that control responsive behavior.

Components
How do you create a responsive navbar in Bootstrap?  
Use .navbar, .navbar-expand-lg, and .navbar-light/dark classes with .collapse for toggling on smaller screens.

What is the purpose of the .container class?  
It centers content and provides responsive padding. Variants: .container-fluid (full width) and .container-{breakpoint}.

Explain Bootstrap buttons.  
Classes like .btn, .btn-primary, .btn-outline-success provide consistent button styles.

How do you implement a modal in Bootstrap?  
Use .modal structure with .modal-dialog and .modal-content. Trigger via data-bs-toggle="modal".

What is a Jumbotron in Bootstrap?  
A large content block for showcasing key information. (Deprecated in Bootstrap 5, replaced by utilities.)

Utilities & Customization
What are Bootstrap utility classes?  
Predefined classes for spacing (.m-3, .p-2), text alignment (.text-center), display (.d-flex), etc.

How do you override Bootstrap styles?  
By writing custom CSS after Bootstrap’s stylesheet or using Sass variables.

Explain the difference between .d-none and .invisible.  
.d-none removes the element from layout, .invisible hides it but keeps space reserved.

How do you align items using Flexbox utilities in Bootstrap?  
Classes like .d-flex, .justify-content-center, .align-items-start.

What is the difference between .container and .container-fluid?  
.container has fixed width at breakpoints, .container-fluid spans full width always.

Advanced
How do you create a responsive table in Bootstrap?  
Wrap table in .table-responsive to enable horizontal scrolling on smaller devices.

Explain Bootstrap’s form validation classes.  
Classes like .is-valid, .is-invalid provide instant feedback styling for form controls.

What is the role of Bootstrap’s JavaScript plugins?  
They add interactivity (modals, tooltips, carousels) using vanilla JS in Bootstrap 5.

How do you use Bootstrap with React or Angular?  
By importing Bootstrap CSS/JS or using libraries like react-bootstrap and ng-bootstrap.

What are Bootstrap Icons?  
A separate icon library introduced in Bootstrap 5, providing scalable vector icons.
